  {"id":"ff296754-4b47-42f7-9ced-5855d13fc1b5","term":"Object divergence metadata","verdict":"MINOR","suggestions":[{"field":"common_mistakes","severity":"Low","issue":"Divergence and object size both widen/diffuse an object and are the two most easily confused parameters in this glossary, yet the mistakes list only contrasts divergence with panning and loudness, not with size. A learner meeting both terms has no cue to tell them apart.","suggestion":"Add a mistake distinguishing the two, e.g. 'Confusing divergence with object size: object size sets the object's spatial extent, while divergence splits its energy to two symmetric points around the stated position.' and add 'Object size metadata' to related_terms so learners can compare the pair."}]},
